cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If Voxora or its measurement data is useful in your research, please cite it."
title: "Voxora: a CPU-only REST API service for speech recognition and synthesis, with measured performance references"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Voxora contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fly88oj/voxora"
url: "https://github.com/fly88oj/voxora"
abstract: >-
  Voxora is a REST API service for speech recognition (ASR) and text-to-speech
  (TTS) that runs entirely on CPU, exposing eight open engines (SenseVoiceSmall,
  streaming Zipformer, Qwen3-ASR, Fun-ASR-Nano, Piper, Qwen3-TTS, CosyVoice3)
  behind one OpenAI-style contract with per-request RTF telemetry. The package
  also ships the measurement harness and reference data behind its performance
  claims: versioned raw results, environment fingerprints including CPU
  affinity and load, a documented TTS-to-ASR round-trip accuracy protocol,
  and a run-to-run stability study.
keywords:
  - speech-recognition
  - text-to-speech
  - api
  - cpu-inference
  - onnx
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1
date-released: "2026-09-22"
